From bea509482907f3ad22acbc11cc5d707fe94f10aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: osrep <osrep@local>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:20:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] add -osrep: content-defined fragments by OSREP (EXPERIMENTAL)

-osrep cuts fragments with OSREP's fragmenter (compressors/osrep, MIT,
plain C99): a gear CDC with min A/2, zpaq's maximum and one threshold,
plus forced cuts after tar headers and zip local headers. -fragment N
means what it means for zpaq's own fragmenter, an average of 2^N KiB;
-osrep without -fragment uses N=3 (8 KiB). zpaq's own default stays 6.

The archive format does not change: the unmodified zpaq-std extracts
every -osrep archive. Without -osrep nothing changes. The plain loop of
add2()/add() and the add2_scan() workers give the same cuts with any
number of threads, because the fragmenter state depends only on the
bytes since the last cut.
